## 5. Key Bugs Encountered & Technical Resolutions

1. **Protoc Shared Library Resolution**: System protoc lacked `libprotoc.so.32` in the standard path. Resolved by creating a wrapper script `/home/pbyanshu/.local/bin/protoc` that exports `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`.
2. **Protobuf Include Directory Paths**: Custom CMake command was configured to generate `.pb.h` directly into `${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/proto` to match `#include "proto/gossip.pb.h"` conventions.
3. **Beast Asynchronous Buffer Lifetimes**: In `HttpProxy::ForwardRequest` and test mocks, request and buffer shared pointers were captured by value in Boost.Beast completion handler lambdas to prevent socket operations on deallocated buffers.
4. **Environment Proxy Interception on Localhost**: Shell environment contained an active `http_proxy` forwarding localhost connections. Resolved by configuring `NO_PROXY="127.0.0.1,localhost"` and unsetting proxy variables in test harnesses.
5. **Node Restart Refutation with Equal Incarnations**: When a node restarted after a crash, peers retained a `DEAD` record at incarnation 0, rejecting `ALIVE` updates at equal incarnation. Resolved by loading persisted incarnation from SQLite on startup and incrementing it ($I \leftarrow I_{\text{persisted}} + 1$), alongside prompt refutation gossip.
6. **Isolated Per-Node SQLite Databases**: NodeAgent defaults database paths to `./data/<node_id>.db`, preventing concurrent database locking and cross-node contamination.

